# Product Overview

hubIO is a modern multi-tenant Property Management SaaS designed to simplify daily operations for apartment owners and property management teams.

The goal is not to build another traditional ERP.

The goal is to create an operating system that makes property management effortless.

Every feature should reduce manual work, increase operational visibility, and improve communication between owners, managers, technicians, housekeepers, and tenants.

---

## Business Domain

hubIO operates in the Property Management Software domain, focusing on operational efficiency rather than accounting or enterprise resource planning.

The product combines multiple domains into a single platform:

* Property Management
* Facility Operations
* Rental Management
* Maintenance Management
* Housekeeping Operations
* Workflow Automation
* Customer Communication
* Multi-tenant SaaS

The primary objective is to centralize day-to-day property operations into one modern operating system that reduces manual work, improves collaboration, and provides complete operational visibility across every property.

---

# Vision

hubIO should become the central operating platform for residential property management.

Users should be able to manage every property from one application.

The product should feel modern, lightweight, and intelligent.

Avoid building complicated enterprise software.

Instead, build software that people actually enjoy using.

---

# Core Product Principles

Every product decision should align with the following principles.

## Dashboard-First

The dashboard is the operational center of the product. Users should immediately understand the health and status of their properties.

## Workflow-Oriented

The product should guide users through complete operational workflows rather than isolated features.

## Multi-Tenant by Default

Every feature must be designed to support multiple properties without architectural changes.

## Simplicity over Complexity

Prefer simple, intuitive workflows over feature-heavy interfaces. Complexity should be hidden whenever possible.

## Mobile-First Operations

Field workers such as technicians and housekeepers primarily use mobile devices. Operational workflows should remain efficient on smaller screens.

## Data-Driven Decisions

Present meaningful operational data that helps users make decisions quickly. Reports and dashboards should prioritize clarity over decoration.

## Automation over Manual Work

Whenever appropriate, the product should automate repetitive operational tasks to reduce human effort and improve consistency.

## Consistent User Experience

Every module should feel like part of the same product by maintaining consistent navigation, interactions, terminology, and visual language.

