# Design Philosophy

The interface should feel like

Linear

Stripe Dashboard

Raycast

Vercel

Notion

Avoid traditional enterprise software appearance.

Avoid outdated admin templates.

Prioritize whitespace.

Use clean typography.

Reduce visual noise.

---

# User Experience Principles

Every page should answer these questions immediately.

Where am I?

What can I do here?

What should I do next?

What changed?

Every primary action must be obvious.

Avoid confusing navigation.

Never hide important actions.

---

# Data Presentation Principles

This is a data-heavy application.

Data should always be easier to scan than to decorate.

Use:

Tables

Cards

Lists

Badges

Status Indicators

Charts only when they provide value.

Avoid unnecessary visualizations.

---

# Multi-Tenant Context

Everything belongs to a Property.

Never assume a single property.

Every entity should be associated with a property when applicable.

Future support for organizations owning hundreds of properties should be possible without redesigning the architecture.

---

# User Interface Expectations

Every screen should include appropriate states.

Loading State

Empty State

Error State

Success State

Permission Denied State (when applicable)

Responsive Layout

Keyboard Accessibility

